 "about": "The rest of what a thing can do to a character, on a second lane. The player starts at x = -17, jumps once at second 3 (a jump to compare with), and is held on D from 5 to 11: a coin at x = -14 hits it (an ability unit of 2000: the health bar read at second 7 is below 10000), a coin at x = -10 gives the status star (invincible), the same hitting coin at x = -6 should now do nothing (the bar read at 9.5 says what it said at 7), a wind at x = -1 blows towards +z (forceField, 6 m/s: the track drifts in z), a big coin at x = 7 pulls (launcher towards the piece, 8 m/s). At 13 the player is put at x = 11, walks through a coin at x = 13 that gives spring (superJump 1 and 2.5) and jumps at 15: the track should rise two and a half times as high as the first jump. Expect HZ_GO, HZ_STING twice, HZ_STAR, HZ_SPRING, and read playerTrack and screenTexts.",
